diff --git a/docs/wiki/decisions/0012-gate-shrink.md b/docs/wiki/decisions/0012-gate-shrink.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..d4a1cc6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/wiki/decisions/0012-gate-shrink.md
@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+---
+type: decision
+status: active
+updated: 2026-11-06
+sources: [.harness/gate-shrink-detail.md, .harness/spike-bprime/RESULTS.md, commit fb40666, commit ba9fa4d, commit 82a05a5, 0005, 0011]
+verified_by: tests/gate.test.sh
+---
+# 0012: Gate shrink: trim the allowlist, keep the gate
+
+**Context.** The "4b" item (0005) wanted the 529-line parser replaced by `permissions` rules plus a small gate. The analyst's usage study (`.harness/gate-shrink-detail.md` §1-3, written against a 552-line gate) counted 754 allowed conductor calls: nearly all were `harness`, `gh pr`, `git status|log|diff --stat|branch`, `cat`/`ls` under `.harness/` and `docs/`, and Read/Write/Glob on `.harness/` and `docs/`. Never used: `git show --stat`, `herdr status|pane list|layout|workspace|tab`, `gh issue|run|repo view|auth|browse|pr status`, `jq` as a pipe consumer (0 of 754 allowed); no filesystem MCP server was configured. The B′ spike (native subagents instead of the harness runner) was rejected on 2026-11-03 (`.harness/spike-bprime/RESULTS.md`): subagents die on conductor exit ("1 local agent couldn't be moved and was stopped"), so the detached runner (0007, 0011) and therefore the gate stay.
+
+**Decision.** Trim, do not replace. Already landed before this step (gate v21): `agent_type` keying, the single-command scanner (`conductor-shell-one-command`), `tests/gate-denied.list` as a regression list. Removed or reduced to the used set: `gh` is `pr create|view|list|checks|comment|edit|merge` only (`--body-file` from `.harness/` or `docs/`, no `merge -d`, no `api`); `git branch` is list-only (`-a -r -v --show-current`); `git show` is denied; `herdr` is `pane get|current`; the Agent/Workflow/Monitor/NotebookEdit tools are in `disallowedTools` of `claude/agents/conductor.md` and no longer in the gate; the `jq` and `mcp__filesystem__*` cases are gone. The policy tables (messages, `BASH_ALLOW`, `GH_ALLOW`, git deny flags) sit in one labelled block at the top. In this step: `--via` (a no-op since step 4) removed from `ask_parse_args` (fb40666), tables labelled (ba9fa4d), gate diagram synced (82a05a5). Gate 552 → 521 lines.
+
+**Kept, and why.** The path helpers (`rel`, `physrel`, `physical`, `readable`, `writable`, `raw_stream_rel`) and the Bash allowlist: they are the only thing that keeps `Read`/`Grep`/`Glob`/`Write` inside `.harness/` and `docs/` after symlink resolution and keeps `.harness/log/*.jsonl` (raw source) unreadable. A `permissions` pattern cannot resolve symlinks or `..`.
+
+**Rejected: option f, `permissions` rules instead of the gate.** User-scope rules bind workers too (the same `~/.claude/settings.json`), so the implementer could not edit source; per-agent scoping exists only in the agent frontmatter, which cannot express path-prefix reads. Project-scope rules are untracked per user and would not follow the opt-in (`harness init`, 0010).
+
+**Status.** Active. Supersedes the 4b consequence in 0005.
+
+**Consequences.** The gate is a routing nudge, not a security boundary (0005). Any new conductor command needs a line in the policy block, a probe in `tests/gate-denied.list` and a line in `conductor.md` "You may run directly". Editing the live gate follows `live-gate-edit` and `in-place-edit-breaks-running-scripts`.
